<title>TURKEY: Turkey to give police further wage rise.</title>
<headline>Turkey to give police further wage rise.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's Finance Minister Abdullatif Sener said on Tuesday police officers would be given a further wage rise on top of a 49 percent increase at the start of the year.</p>
<p>Sener declined to state the size of the rise but finance officials said it would be between five and six percent. Annual inflation in Turkey is around 80 percent.</p>
<p>Speaking to journalists, Sener also said a proposal to increase civil servant pension payments had been presented to ministers for their approval.</p>
<p>-- Ankara Newsroom +90-312-446 2940</p>
